{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f71387d9-cdc7-4291-91ab-88ffc5025d1e","agentId":"aa2deafc5c0109a11","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Task: obtain manufacturer 3D CAD models (STEP) for standard catalog parts used in the AUTOKITCH machine's electrical layer, so the model uses real parts instead of simplified boxes. The project owner (Kemal) explicitly asked: \"use that site with the 3D models of motors etc., take everything from there, standard real parts\" — the site is TraceParts (www.traceparts.com); the project's existing catalog STEP library is in\nC:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE\\AUTOKITCH_COORDINATION\\worktrees\\claude-hat3-v3\\arastirma\\katalog\\step (each STEP has a companion .txt with the TraceParts attribute export: TraceParts.PartNumber, REFERENCE, SUPPLIER…). Follow that convention.\n\nSave NEW files ONLY into: C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\scratchpad\\katalog_v34\\  (create it). Name files by the manufacturer order number (lowercase, e.g. 53111020.stp) and write a small .txt next to each with: manufacturer, order no., title, source URL, date, and the key dimensions you can read.\n\nParts wanted (priority order):\n1. Lapp SKINTOP ST-M cable glands: 53111010 (M16), 53111020 (M20), 53111040 (M32); Lapp SKINTOP MS-M 32 (multi-hole capable) and locknuts SKINTOP GMP-GL-M 53119010 (M16), 53119020 (M20).\n2. icotek cable entry frames: KEL-DPZ 16|14 (43816), KEL 10|3 (42212.200), grommet KT 20 (41220).\n3. Hager tehalit BA7A slotted wiring duct: BA7A40030, BA7A40040, BA7A40060 (any length; duct is a prismatic section, a short length is fine).\n4. NORMA RSGU1 W5 P-clips 12 mm band: 0941 7712 006/008/010/012 (Ø6/8/10/12).\n5. Control/panel devices: Kunbus RevPi Connect 4 PR100378, Phoenix Contact FL SWITCH 1008N 1085256, Schneider A9S65440 / A9R21440 / A9F79616, Mean Well NDR-120-24, Murrelektronik Exact12 8000-88460-0000000.\n\nHow: use a browser. Prefer the user's Chrome via the claude-in-chrome tools (the user may already be logged into TraceParts there; load them with ToolSearch first — query \"select:mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__navigate,mcp__claude-in-chrome__computer,mcp__claude-in-chrome__read_page,mcp__claude-in-chrome__find,mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp,mcp__claude-in-chrome__get_page_text\"). If Chrome is not available use the built-in browser tools (mcp__Claude_Browser__*). If a download is offered directly by the manufacturer's own site (Lapp, Phoenix, Schneider, Mean Well, Murrelektronik, icotek), that is also acceptable (manufacturer source = OK; community sites like GrabCAD/Cults are NOT acceptable).\nRULES: Do NOT create accounts, do NOT type any password or credentials, do NOT accept paid offers. If a site requires login and there is no existing logged-in session, skip it and report that. Decline non-essential cookies when a banner appears. Downloads are authorized only for these catalog CAD files. Downloaded browser files usually land in the user's Downloads folder (C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Downloads) — move/copy them (unzip if needed) into the katalog_v34 folder. Do not edit any project files.\nTime-box: about 30 minutes. Return a table: part | file saved (path) | source URL | status (OK / login required / not found) and any notes on sizes."},"uuid":"416ea596-06b7-496b-a264-ef1f27883b75","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:26:27.464Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
