{"parentUuid":"db9a0f2d-a772-4fd6-a738-792c5141f7d2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa2deafc5c0109a11","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14798423 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8ad5ccae-9f33-4c21-be15-3cc4102322c5","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:46:07.321Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14798423 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
{"parentUuid":"8ad5ccae-9f33-4c21-be15-3cc4102322c5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa2deafc5c0109a11","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbcsxLWbikfH4NDkA7F2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I got 5 of the 16 parts as real manufacturer STEP files, all from group 5 (control/panel devices). None of the cable-gland, cable-entry, wiring-duct or P-clip parts (groups 1–4) were downloaded. TraceParts needs a login, there was no existing session in Chrome, and I did not sign in.\n\nFiles are in `C:\\Users\\Kemal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-Kemal-Desktop-Kemal-WEBS-TE\\f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8\\scratchpad\\katalog_v34\\`. Each STEP has a .txt next to it with manufacturer, order no., title, source URL, date and size. I measured the sizes from the STEP files themselves; they include terminals and DIN clips, so they run a bit larger than the catalog figures.\n\n| Part | File saved | Source | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Lapp SKINTOP ST-M 53111010 / 53111020 / 53111040, MS-M 32, GMP-GL-M 53119010 / 53119020 | none | TraceParts (only listed through the distributor RS Group) and Lapp's own CAD portal (lapp.partcommunity.com, run by CADENAS) | Login required on both |\n| icotek KEL-DPZ 16\\|14 (43816), KEL 10\\|3 (42212.200), KT 20 (41220) | none | icotek.com | Not found: the site search returned \"No results\" even for 43816 |\n| Hager tehalit BA7A40030 / 40040 / 40060 | none | — | Not tried (time box) |\n| NORMA RSGU1 W5 0941 7712 006/008/010/012 | none | — | Not tried (time box) |\n| Kunbus RevPi Connect 4 PR100378 | `pr100378.stp` (with WLAN) and `pr100378_without_wlan.stp` | revolutionpi.com/fileadmin/downloads/step_files/RevPi-Connect-4.zip | OK |\n| Phoenix FL SWITCH 1008N 1085256 | `1085256.stp` (.txt also has the TraceParts attribute export from the zip) | phoenixcontact.com/en-pc/products/industrial-ethernet-switch-fl-switch-1008n-1085256 | OK |\n| Schneider A9S65440 (iSW 4P 40 A) | `a9s65440.stp` | se.com/uk/en/product/A9S65440/ | OK |\n| Schneider A9R21440 (iID 4P 40 A 30 mA type A) | `a9r21440.stp` | se.com/uk/en/product/A9R21440/ | OK |\n| Schneider A9F79616 | none | se.com UK / IT / FR / AE | Not found: that reference sends you to the product overview on all four country sites |\n| Mean Well NDR-120-24 | `ndr-120-24.stp` (one model for the whole NDR-120 series) | meanwell.com/upload/pdf/NDR-120/NDR-120-3D.zip | OK |\n| Murrelektronik Exact12 8000-88460-0000000 | none | shop.murrelektronik.com (file 8000-88460-0000000_stp_x_a.zip) | Blocked: the download needs an \"I agree with the Privacy Policy and Legal Notice\" box ticked, and I don't tick terms without Kemal's own OK |\n\n**Sizes (width on DIN rail first, mm):**\n- **FL SWITCH 1008N:** 22.5 × 147.6 × 98.4 (height includes the DIN latch).\n- **A9S65440:** 71.8 × 93.9 × 75.1 (catalog 72 × 85 × 73).\n- **A9R21440:** 73.6 × 95.4 × 74.4 (72 mm, 8 modules).\n- **NDR-120:** 40 × 124.3 × 129.2 (catalog 40 × 125.2 × 113.5).\n- **RevPi Connect 4:** 45 × 114.6 × 96.8 with WLAN, 45 × 110.6 × 96.8 without.\n\n**Things to decide or check:**\n- **PR100378:** Kunbus ships two STEP files and I couldn't confirm which one PR100378 is. Keep the one that matches and delete the other. Both are about 25 MB of detailed board geometry, so they need simplifying before going into the GLB.\n- **A9F79616:** the order number is probably mistyped and should be checked.\n- **Lapp and other login-only parts:** if Kemal signs in to TraceParts or Lapp's CAD portal in his own Chrome, they can be fetched in a later pass.\n- **Murrelektronik:** he can tick the terms box himself and download.\n- **Phoenix \"I am human\" check:** the Phoenix download has one. It ticked itself in the background and I didn't interact with it.\n- **Downloads folder:** Chrome saved the browser downloads there as `.tmp` files (`658909c7-….tmp`, `82b07af9-….tmp`, `6364bc3a-….tmp`). I copied them and left the originals; they can be deleted.\n\nNo project files were edited. The raw zips are in `scratchpad\\_zip_v34_raw\\`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":288,"cache_read_input_tokens":201355,"output_tokens":1782,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":288},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1782,"cache_read_input_tokens":201355,"cache_creation_input_tokens":288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":288,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfbcswURngcBjeXJv7Bho","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionMcpServer":"claude-in-chrome","attributionMcpTool":"tabs_close_mcp","type":"assistant","uuid":"bf615f5d-e1cb-417e-9a7e-b9dab03fe7e3","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:46:24.229Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Kemal\\Desktop\\Kemal\\WEBSİTE","sessionId":"f3ef876a-f062-4b29-bb81-775cc8a1a6d8","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"crystalline-crunching-moonbeam"}
